Subject: [PATCH 40/59] Question detail returns the run state only to full
 viewers (K1)

QuestionService.detail() returned the whole question_runs row to every viewer
can_view admits, including a holder owner who was only routed the question.
Since C1 the checkpoint state carries text derived from every holder's response
(gate_notes competing/verification_competing, verified, investigation notes), so
a routed-only owner could read the other side's values.

detail() now returns the run state only when the viewer is a full viewer (the
flag that already filters responses). Everyone else gets the run's question_id,
tenant_id, step, attempts and updated_at with an empty state.

Regression tests (REVIEWER-2 probe P4): a routed-only owner on the rival side
sees no value, competing or verification_competing text; a full viewer still
gets the state unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
